codex
A raw-text pinning check exposed only a surface-syntax difference: the translator elides empty statement lists, while the claim spells them as `.Stmts`. Because K parses both to the same term, I’m replacing that textual check with a parser-level KAST identity check before drawing any fidelity conclusion. The concrete result substitutions already agree for every witness tested.
